ITEMS = ((('what should i do during an asthma attack', 'how do i help someone with asthma', 'what is the first aid for asthma', 'how to respond to an asthma attack', 'what to do when asthma gets worse', 'how do you handle asthma symptoms', 'what helps a person with asthma', 'how can i assist during an asthma attack', 'what is the best response to asthma', 'how should i care for someone with asthma'), 'For an asthma attack, help the person sit upright and use their prescribed reliever inhaler as directed. Keep calm and loosen tight clothing. Call emergency services if symptoms do not improve, breathing is very difficult or the person is tired.'), (('how do i know if asthma is getting worse with asthma', 'what are the signs of a severe asthma attack', 'how to tell mild from serious asthma', 'what symptoms of asthma need urgent help', 'how does severe asthma feel', 'what if the reliever is not working with asthma', 'how to recognise life threatening asthma', 'what if the person cannot speak in sentences with asthma', 'how to judge breathing in asthma', 'who can assess worsening asthma'), 'Worsening asthma may mean the reliever is not helping, breathlessness at rest, difficulty speaking, blue lips or exhaustion. Call emergency services straight away. A silent chest or drowsiness is a sign of a very serious attack.'), (('how should someone sit during an asthma attack', 'what position helps breathing in asthma', 'should i lie a person down with asthma', 'how to support someone with asthma', 'should i loosen clothing for asthma', 'what if the person wants to stand with asthma', 'how to keep an asthma patient calm', 'what if symptoms worsen while sitting with asthma', 'how to help a child with asthma sit', 'who can advise about positioning with asthma'), 'Sit the person upright and let them lean forward slightly if that eases breathing. Loosen tight clothing and stay calm with them. Call emergency services if they cannot settle or are becoming tired.'), (('should i use a spacer with an inhaler with asthma', 'how to help someone use an inhaler with asthma', 'what if i cannot find their inhaler with asthma', "can i borrow someone else's inhaler with asthma", 'how many puffs for an asthma attack', 'what to do if the inhaler is empty with asthma', 'should i ask about a reliever inhaler with asthma', 'what if a child cannot use an inhaler with asthma', 'how to check an inhaler is working with asthma', 'who can advise about inhaler technique with asthma'), 'Help the person use their own prescribed reliever inhaler, and a spacer if they have one, following the instructions they were given. Do not borrow an inhaler from someone else. Call emergency services if relief is not sustained.'), (('when should i call an ambulance for asthma', 'is an asthma attack always an emergency', 'what if asthma does not improve', 'should i call for mild asthma symptoms', 'what to tell the operator about asthma', 'how urgent is a bad asthma attack', 'what if the person is drowsy with asthma', 'should i call after the attack settles with asthma', 'when to seek help at night with asthma', 'who decides if asthma needs help'), 'Call an ambulance if the reliever is not working, breathing is severe, the person is drowsy or cannot speak, or symptoms worsen. Tell the operator how long the attack has lasted. Stay with the person and keep them calm.'), (('what triggers an asthma attack', 'can exercise trigger asthma', 'does cold air make asthma worse', 'what allergens affect asthma', 'can smoke trigger asthma', 'what if asthma follows a cold', 'how to avoid asthma triggers', 'why does asthma happen at night', 'when to ask a doctor about triggers with asthma', 'who can help identify asthma triggers'), 'Asthma can be triggered by colds, exercise, cold air, smoke, dust or pollen. Avoiding known triggers and using prescribed preventer treatment can reduce attacks. Ask a doctor or nurse to review asthma if attacks are frequent.'), (('how do i help a child with asthma', 'what to do for asthma in a toddler', 'can babies have asthma', 'how to spot asthma symptoms in children', 'should i call help for a child with asthma', 'how to use a spacer for a child with asthma', 'what if a child is too breathless to speak with asthma', 'how to keep a child calm during asthma', 'when to take a child to hospital for asthma', "who can review a child's asthma"), 'Sit the child upright, help them use their own reliever inhaler with a spacer if available, and stay calm. Call emergency services if they are breathless at rest, drowsy or not improving. A doctor should review frequent symptoms.'), (('what if an asthma patient becomes unconscious', 'should i start cpr for asthma', 'how to respond to a collapsed person with asthma', 'what to do if breathing stops with asthma', 'how to check breathing in asthma', 'what if the person stops responding with asthma', 'should i fetch a defibrillator with asthma', 'how to hand over to paramedics with asthma', 'what to tell the crew about the attack with asthma', 'who takes over from me with asthma first aid'), 'If a person with asthma becomes unresponsive and is not breathing normally, call emergency services and start CPR. Tell the crew about the attack and any treatment used. Continue until a qualified person arrives.'), (('can asthma be cured', 'how is asthma managed long term', 'what is a preventer inhaler for with asthma', 'should i carry a reliever every day with asthma', 'how to make an asthma action plan', 'when to review asthma treatment', 'what if i use my reliever often with asthma', 'how to live well with asthma', 'who can write an asthma plan', 'what follow up is needed with asthma'), 'Asthma is usually managed rather than cured, with preventer and reliever medicines and a written action plan. Ask a doctor or nurse to review treatment if you use the reliever often. Carry your reliever with you and know when to call for help.'), (('what not to do during an asthma attack with asthma', 'should i give water during asthma', 'can i lay someone flat with asthma', 'is it bad to panic during an attack with asthma', 'should i use herbal remedies for asthma', 'what if i cannot find their medicine with asthma', 'should i leave someone alone with asthma', 'what if i try to force breathing with asthma', 'when to avoid waiting it out with asthma', 'who can advise on asthma first aid'), 'Do not lay the person flat, give food or drink, or leave them alone during an asthma attack. Do not rely on home remedies instead of prescribed treatment. Call emergency services if symptoms are severe or not improving.'))
